  "Question": "If the length of a rectangle is increased by \\(20\\%\\) and its width is increased by \\(50\\%,\\) then the area is increased by",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(70\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(80\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(100\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Increasing the length by \\(20\\%\\) makes it \\(120\\%=1.2\\) times its original length. Increasing the width by \\(50\\%\\) makes it \\(150\\%=1.5\\) times its original width.\n\nSince a rectangle's area is length times width, the new area is\n\\[\n1.2\\times1.5=1.8\n\\]\ntimes the original area. Of this, \\(1\\) is the original area, leaving an increase of \\(1.8-1=0.8=80\\%\\). The answer is \\(80\\%\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
